id: called-shot
name: Called Shot
type: modifier
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerTier: 2
usageLimit: 1/round
baseManeuver: attacking
baseForbids: area
damageCategoryShift: 1
strikePerTier: -2
asks: State the area you targeted
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Aim for something in particular. One Damage Category harder, 2(T) off the Strike
  Roll, and the area you called is on the card for the ARC to rule on.
text: >
  Called Shot [1/Round]: A unique type of Maneuver that allows you to target
  specific weaknesses.
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Base Maneuver: Any Attacking Maneuver.
  –KP Cost: 2(T)
  –Effect: At Attack Declaration, when making an Attacking Maneuver that does not
  have an Area of Effect, you can use this Maneuver to increase the Damage Category
  of that Attacking Maneuver by 1 but decrease the Strike Roll for that Attacking
  Maneuver by 2(T).
  State the area you targeted with this Attacking Maneuver. Your ARC may allow for
  special effects to occur if you knock that Opponent through a Health Threshold or
  deal Damage equal to or exceeding 1/5th of that target’s Maximum Life Points. A
  few potential example targets are:

  * Head: That Character gains the Impediment Combat Condition until the start of
    your next turn.
  * Eyes: That Character gains the Blinded Combat Condition until the end of their
    next turn.
  * Arm: That Character gains the Guard Down Combat Condition until the start of
    your next turn.
  * Leg: That Character has their Speeds and Defense Value halved until the start of
    your next turn.
  * Gut: That Character is knocked Prone.

---

# No script, and none wanted. What this Maneuver does to an attack is two numbers and
# a question, and all three are said in the header:
#
#   damageCategoryShift: 1     "increase the Damage Category of that Attacking
#                               Maneuver by 1"
#   strikePerTier: -2          "decrease the Strike Roll for that Attacking Maneuver
#                               by 2(T)"
#   asks: ...                  "state the area you targeted with this Attacking
#                               Maneuver"
#
# Said in the header rather than given a flag and a branch in the code, because this is
# the first Modifier Maneuver and the next one should need no code at all. A Modifier
# that shifts a Category and takes something off a Strike is a shape, not a special
# case.
#
# `baseForbids: area` is the other half of the condition. The Base Maneuver line says
# "any Attacking Maneuver" and the Effect narrows it to "that does not have an Area of
# Effect", so the two are written separately: what it applies to, and what it will not
# apply to.
#
# --- What the ARC decides ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Your ARC may allow for special effects to occur if you knock that Opponent through
# a Health Threshold or deal Damage equal to or exceeding 1/5th of that target's
# Maximum Life Points."
#
# That is a ruling, not a rule: "may allow", and the five below it are "a few potential
# example targets" rather than a list to choose from. So the area you called is written
# on the card in your own words, where the ARC and the table can see it, and what it
# comes to is theirs. Nothing here picks a Condition off that list, because the entry
# does not say that hitting the Head applies Impediment - it says an ARC may decide it
# does.
#
# The two thresholds it names are both visible without being asked for: a Health
# Threshold crossed is announced by the system already, and the Damage dealt is on the
# card beside the target's Life Points.
